-      "title": "PDPA data breach notification workflow with 72-hour commissioner deadline",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Malaysia's amended PDPA (Phase 3, June 2025) mandates that data controllers notify the Personal Data Protection Commissioner within 72 hours of discovering a qualifying breach, and notify affected data subjects within 7 days. Rainbow AI stores WhatsApp message history and guest personal data, requiring a documented breach response workflow.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A new admin endpoint `POST /api/rainbow/security/breach-report` accepts a breach description and creates a timestamped breach record in a `pdpa_breach_log` table",
-        "On creation, the system automatically calculates and stores the 72-hour commissioner notification deadline and 7-day subject notification deadline",
-        "Admin WhatsApp notification is sent to the system admin with breach details and both deadlines",
-        "Admin dashboard shows open breach records with countdown timers to each deadline, colour-coded (green/amber/red)",
-        "Breach log is append-only; contains: reported_by, description, affected_count_estimate, commissioner_notified_at (nullable), subjects_notified_at (nullable)",
-        "A daily cron job checks for overdue notifications and sends a reminder alert if deadlines are approaching within 6 hours"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Lightweight workflow management — no external PDPC API integration required (notification is done manually by admin, system tracks deadlines)",
-        "Create `src/routes/admin/breach-report.ts` following the same pattern as `src/routes/admin/gdpr-erasure.ts`",
-        "Use existing `admin-notifier.ts` for the WhatsApp alert"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": true
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-840",
-      "title": "WhatsApp media message acknowledgement in AI conversation flow",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Guests frequently send images (booking confirmations, screenshots, receipts) and voice notes to the hostel WhatsApp. Rainbow AI currently only processes text messages and silently ignores media. Acknowledging media receipt with a context-aware response prevents users from thinking their message was lost.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Incoming image messages trigger a configurable static reply from the `media_received` static reply key",
-        "Incoming audio/voice messages trigger a separate static reply from the `audio_received` key",
-        "Incoming document messages trigger a `document_received` reply",
-        "Media messages are logged to `rainbow_messages` with `messageType: 'image'|'audio'|'document'` and `mediaUrl` (if available)",
-        "The feature is configurable per-profile: `features.mediaRepliesEnabled: true|false` in settings.json",
-        "Media replies do not count against conversation fallback rate metrics"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Add media type detection in `src/assistant/pipeline/input-validator.ts` based on `IncomingMessage.messageType`",
-        "The `messageType` field already exists on `IncomingMessage` in `src/assistant/types.ts`",
-        "Route media messages to a dedicated `media-handler` stage that short-circuits the full NLP pipeline"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": true
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-841",
-      "title": "Webchat widget consent banner with timestamped opt-in log",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "The webchat widget collects and processes personal data (chat content) without presenting a data processing consent notice. GDPR and Malaysia's PDPA both require explicit informed consent before initiating data collection. Industry audits find 47% of chatbots lack this, representing a compliance vulnerability.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "On first widget load, a consent banner is shown before the chat interface with [Accept] and [Decline] options",
-        "If the user declines, the chat interface is not rendered and a privacy policy link is shown",
-        "If the user accepts, the acceptance is stored in `localStorage` with timestamp and not shown again for 365 days",
-        "The consent timestamp and a truncated session ID are sent to `POST /api/webchat/consent-log` and persisted to DB",
-        "The consent banner is keyboard-accessible and meets WCAG 2.1 AA",
-        "Consent text content is configurable per profile via admin settings"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Add consent check at the top of `src/public/js/modules/chat-send.js` before any message is sent",
-        "Consent log table: `webchat_consent_log(session_id_hash, accepted_at, profile_id, user_agent_hash)`",
-        "Use `localStorage.setItem('rb_consent', JSON.stringify({accepted: true, ts: Date.now()}))` for persistence"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": true
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-842",
-      "title": "Baileys DB auth state health check and corruption recovery at startup",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Baileys session credentials stored in PostgreSQL can become corrupted during a crash mid-transaction. The next reconnection attempt will silently fail with a malformed session error, requiring manual DB intervention. An automatic health check at startup should detect and clear corrupted auth state before attempting connection.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "At server startup, before calling `makeWASocket`, a `validateAuthState(instanceId)` check queries DB auth rows and verifies JSON parseability of credential fields",
-        "If validation fails (unparseable JSON, missing required creds fields), corrupted rows are deleted and the QR pairing flow is re-initiated",
-        "An admin WhatsApp notification is sent: '[instanceId] auth state was corrupted and cleared — please re-scan QR code'",
-        "Validation results are logged at INFO level: `[DbAuth:pelangi] Auth state healthy: creds OK, 42 signal keys`",
-        "A new admin endpoint `GET /api/rainbow/instances/:id/auth-health` returns auth state validity without triggering recovery"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Add `validateAuthState(instanceId: string)` to `src/lib/whatsapp/db-auth-state.ts`",
-        "Check: `SELECT key, value FROM wa_auth_state WHERE instance_id = $1` — attempt `JSON.parse(value)` for each row",
-        "Required credential fields for a valid Baileys session: `noiseKey`, `signedIdentityKey`, `registrationId`, `advSecretKey`",
-        "Call validation from `WhatsAppInstance.start()` before `useDbAuthState()` in `src/lib/whatsapp/instance.ts`"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": true
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-843",
-      "title": "Structured data notice sent to user on first WhatsApp interaction",
-      "priority": "low",
-      "description": "When a guest initiates their first WhatsApp conversation with the bot, they receive no notification that their messages will be stored and processed. PDPA's Notice and Choice Principle requires data subjects to be informed of collection purposes at or before collection.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "On the very first message from a new JID (no prior `rainbow_conversations` record), a data notice follows the normal welcome response",
