-    {
-      "id": "US-844",
-      "title": "Webhook HMAC signature validation for incoming Meta Cloud API events",
-      "priority": "low",
-      "description": "Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API signs incoming webhook payloads with HMAC-SHA256 using the app secret. Without signature validation, the webhook endpoint accepts any HTTP POST, allowing malicious actors to inject fake template status updates, quality rating changes, or delivery receipts. The raw body capture is already in place.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "All requests to `POST /webhooks/meta` are rejected with HTTP 403 if the `X-Hub-Signature-256` header is absent or invalid",
-        "Validation computes `hmac-sha256(APP_SECRET, rawBody)` and compares with the header value using constant-time comparison",
-        "When validation fails, the rejection is logged at WARN level with the source IP",
-        "If `META_APP_SECRET` environment variable is not set, validation is skipped with a startup WARNING log",
-        "A unit test covers: valid signature passes, tampered body fails, missing header fails"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "`req.rawBody` is already captured in `src/index.ts` via `captureRawBody` middleware",
-        "Add `validateMetaSignature(req)` middleware to `src/routes/webhooks/index.ts`",
-        "Use `crypto.timingSafeEqual()` for constant-time comparison to prevent timing attacks",
-        "Header format: `X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=<hex-digest>`"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": true
-    },
